### ====================================================================
### RepoRadar Server REST API - Test Requests (Module 2: Auth + Protected CRUD)
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension, Postman, or curl
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@projectId = 65d75cf9e1d84f23b890abcd

# Set this after calling POST /api/auth/login
@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### 1. Server Root Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### ====================================================================
### Authentication Endpoints (Module 2)
### ====================================================================

### 3. Register a New User
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kunal Saini",
  "email": "kunal@reporadar.io",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 4. Login User (Obtains JWT Token for NextAuth Credentials & API calls)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kunal@reporadar.io",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 5. Get Current User Profile (Protected with Bearer Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ====================================================================
### Protected Project Resource Endpoints (Requires Authorization Header)
### ====================================================================

### 6. Create Project - Success (Protected)
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RepoRadar Core Engine",
  "description": "AI-powered AST static analysis and vulnerability scanning pipeline"
}

### 7. List All Projects (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get Project By ID (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Update Project (Protected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RepoRadar Core Engine (Updated v1.2)",
  "description": "Updated description with enhanced multi-language AST support"
}

### 10. Delete Project (Protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ====================================================================
### Validation & Auth Error Test Cases
### ====================================================================

### 11. Auth Error: Call Protected Endpoint without Token (Expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Accept: application/json

### 12. Auth Error: Call Protected Endpoint with Invalid Token (Expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token-12345
Accept: application/json

### 13. Auth Error: Login with Wrong Password (Expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kunal@reporadar.io",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 14. Validation Error: Register with short password (Expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@reporadar.io",
  "password": "123"
}
